    </nav>

    <section class="section-wrap" style="padding-top:35px;padding-bottom:35px"><div style="background:var(--paper);padding:28px;border-left:4px solid var(--gold-text)"><p class="eyebrow">New · The growing Sintra directory</p><h2 style="font:500 clamp(27px,4vw,40px) var(--font-serif);margin:12px 0">30 places, free discoveries, food and seasonal events.</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.8">Explore a curated and searchable companion to this guide, with direct maps, practical tips, suggested routes and a dated events diary.</p><a class="button" href="sintra-local-discoveries.html">Explore the Sintra directory ↗</a></div></section>
    <section class="section-wrap" style="padding-top:18px;padding-bottom:18px"><div style="background:var(--forest);color:var(--ivory);padding:24px 28px;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:18px;flex-wrap:wrap"><div><p class="eyebrow" style="color:var(--gold-light);margin:0 0 8px">A slower way to experience Sintra</p><h2 style="font:500 clamp(25px,4vw,36px) var(--font-serif);margin:0 0 6px">Discover our romantic field guide.</h2><p style="margin:0;color:rgba(244,238,223,.8);font-size:13px;line-height:1.7">Gardens, quiet paths, palaces and thoughtful itineraries for two.</p></div><a class="button" href="sintra-romantic-guide.html" style="white-space:nowrap">Explore the romantic guide ↗</a></div></section>
    <section class="guide-intro section-wrap" id="first-look">
      <p class="eyebrow">01 · Get your bearings</p>
      <h2>Let Sintra set<br><em>its own rhythm.</em></h2>
      <p>Sintra is not a place to squeeze into a hurried checklist. The historic centre, the forested hills and the monuments sit across a landscape that takes time to cross. Choose fewer stops, book timed entries carefully and leave room for the town itself.</p>
      <div class="guide-facts">
        <div><strong>Allow</strong><span>A full day for a first visit</span></div>
        <div><strong>Bring</strong><span>Comfortable shoes and a light layer</span></div>
        <div><strong>Expect</strong><span>Steep paths, changing weather and crowds</span></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="guide-highlights" id="highlights">
      <div class="section-wrap">
        <p class="eyebrow">02 · Choose your stops</p>
        <h2>Four places, four different moods.</h2>
        <div class="highlight-grid">
          <article class="highlight-card"><span class="highlight-no">01</span><h3>Palácio da Pena</h3><p>The unmistakable hilltop palace. Its colours and terraces are spectacular, but the visit works best when you respect your timed entry and allow time to reach the palace from the park entrance.</p><a href="https://www.parquesdesintra.pt/pt/parques-monumentos/parque-e-palacio-nacional-da-pena/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Official visitor information ↗</a></article>
          <article class="highlight-card"><span class="highlight-no">02</span><h3>Quinta da Regaleira</h3><p>A romantic estate of gardens, grottoes, tunnels and symbolic architecture. Give the gardens time; the Initiation Well is only one part of the experience.</p><a href="https://www.regaleira.pt/pt/visitas" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Official visitor information ↗</a></article>
          <article class="highlight-card"><span class="highlight-no">03</span><h3>Castelo dos Mouros</h3><p>Come for the long stone walls and the views across the hills. There are uneven steps and exposed sections, so take your time and check the weather.</p><a href="https://www.parquesdesintra.pt/pt/parques-monumentos/castelo-dos-mouros/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Official visitor information ↗</a></article>
          <article class="highlight-card"><span class="highlight-no">04</span><h3>Palácio de Monserrate</h3><p>A quieter-feeling alternative for architecture and gardens, with an extraordinary blend of styles. It deserves more than a quick photo stop.</p><a href="https://www.parquesdesintra.pt/pt/parques-monumentos/parque-e-palacio-de-monserrate/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Official visitor information ↗</a></article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="guide-intro section-wrap" id="getting-around">
      <p class="eyebrow">03 · Move around wisely</p>
      <h2>Sintra is small on the map.<br><em>Not on the ground.</em></h2>
      <p>The monuments sit across the hills, not in one walkable cluster. The easiest plan is usually to arrive by train, use the local public transport or walk where the route makes sense, and avoid trying to drive from monument to monument.</p>
      <div class="guide-facts">
        <div><strong>By train</strong><span>Direct services connect Lisbon with Sintra. Check the timetable before setting off.</span></div>
        <div><strong>By bus</strong><span>Bus 434 serves the historic centre, Moorish Castle and Pena area. Check the operator’s current route and ticket conditions.</span></div>
        <div><strong>By car</strong><span>Private vehicles are restricted on access roads to Pena and in parts of the historic centre. Use designated parking and continue on foot or by public transport.</span></div>
      </div>
      <p style="margin-top:28px"><a class="text-link" href="https://www.parquesdesintra.pt/pt/planear-a-visita/como-chegar/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Check the official access and transport guidance ↗</a></p>
    </section>

    <section class="guide-highlights" id="plan">
      <div class="section-wrap">
        <p class="eyebrow">05 · Choose your pace</p>
        <h2>Two ways to spend your time.</h2>
        <div class="highlight-grid">
          <article class="highlight-card"><span class="highlight-no">ONE DAY · FIRST VISIT</span><h3>The essential Sintra day</h3><p><strong>Morning:</strong> Book an early timed entry at Pena and allow time for the walk or transfer from the park entrance to the palace. <strong>Lunch:</strong> Return towards the historic centre and take a proper break. <strong>Afternoon:</strong> Visit Quinta da Regaleira if you have enough time and a suitable ticket slot. Keep the rest of the afternoon flexible.</p><p><strong>Best for:</strong> First-time visitors who want to experience two signature places without racing between every monument.</p></article>
          <article class="highlight-card"><span class="highlight-no">TWO DAYS · SLOWER EXPLORATION</span><h3>More gardens, less rushing</h3><p><strong>Day one:</strong> Explore Pena and the Moorish Castle, allowing time for the hill paths and viewpoints. Finish in the historic centre. <strong>Day two:</strong> Give Quinta da Regaleira a generous visit, then choose Monserrate for its gardens and architecture. Check transport connections before committing to the order.</p><p><strong>Best for:</strong> Travellers who enjoy gardens, architecture and a more relaxed pace.</p></article>
        </div>
        <p class="guide-disclaimer">These are planning frameworks, not timed guarantees. Check each attraction’s entry slot, travel time and current access conditions before booking. Avoid buying consecutive timed entries at different monuments unless you have confirmed the transfer.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="guide-intro section-wrap" id="food">
      <p class="eyebrow">06 · A taste of Sintra</p>
      <h2>Save room for<br><em>something sweet.</em></h2>
      <p>Sintra has its own pastry traditions. Look out for two classics in the village: <strong>travesseiros</strong>, flaky pastries traditionally filled with an almond-and-egg cream, and <strong>queijadas</strong>, small cheese-based tarts with a lightly spiced, caramelised finish. They are part of the town’s food identity, not just souvenirs.</p>
      <div class="guide-facts">
        <div><strong>Travesseiro</strong><span>Best enjoyed freshly made, ideally still slightly warm.</span></div>
        <div><strong>Queijada</strong><span>A small traditional tart with a rich, gently sweet filling.</span></div>
        <div><strong>Local tip</strong><span>Take a break in the historic centre rather than trying to eat between bus connections.</span></div>
      </div>
      <p style="margin-top:28px"><a class="text-link" href="https://visitsintra.travel/en" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Explore the official Visit Sintra guide ↗</a></p>
    </section>

    <section class="guide-plan section-wrap" id="day-plan">
      <p class="eyebrow">09 · A realistic first day</p>
      <h2>One day in Sintra.<br><em>Without the sprint.</em></h2>
      <p class="plan-lead">A suggested structure, not a race. Pick two major monuments rather than trying to see everything in one day.</p>
      <div class="timeline">
        <article><span>Morning</span><div><h3>Start with your timed ticket</h3><p>Visit the monument you most want to see first. For many first-time visitors, that is Pena or Regaleira. Check the official entry time and transport before leaving.</p></div></article>
        <article><span>Midday</span><div><h3>Pause in the historic centre</h3><p>Walk through the old town, have lunch and make time for a pastry. Avoid planning a tight transfer between timed entries.</p></div></article>
        <article><span>Afternoon</span><div><h3>Choose one more experience</h3><p>Regaleira, the Moorish Castle or Monserrate can each fill a meaningful part of the afternoon. Choose according to your interests and energy.</p></div></article>
        <article><span>Late day</span><div><h3>Leave space for the unexpected</h3><p>Return to the village, browse slowly and check your return transport. The last part of the day should not depend on a risky connection.</p></div></article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="guide-highlights" id="photographs">
