          <figure class="photo-card"><img src="https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Regaleira_Initiation_Well.JPG/960px-Regaleira_Initiation_Well.JPG" alt="The Initiation Well at Quinta da Regaleira"><figcaption><strong>Quinta da Regaleira</strong>Photo: Husond · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Regaleira_Initiation_Well.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Original file and licence</a></figcaption></figure>
          <figure class="photo-card"><img src="https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/28/Castelo_dos_Mouros._Sintra%2C_Portugal.jpg/960px-Castelo_dos_Mouros._Sintra%2C_Portugal.jpg" alt="Stone walls of Castelo dos Mouros above Sintra"><figcaption><strong>Moorish Castle</strong>Photo: Ввласенко · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Castelo_dos_Mouros._Sintra,_Portugal.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Original file and licence</a></figcaption></figure>
          <figure class="photo-card"><img src="https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0c/Pal%C3%A1cio_de_Monserrate_DSC08899_%2836939236406%29.jpg/960px-Pal%C3%A1cio_de_Monserrate_DSC08899_%2836939236406%29.jpg" alt="Ornate exterior of Palácio de Monserrate"><figcaption><strong>Monserrate Palace</strong>Photo: nborges · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pal%C3%A1cio_de_Monserrate_DSC08899_(36939236406).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Original file and licence</a></figcaption></figure>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="guide-highlights" id="tickets">
      <div class="section-wrap">
        <p class="eyebrow">07 · Plan your budget</p>
        <h2>Know what your tickets cover.</h2>
        <p class="plan-lead">Adult reference prices currently published by the operators, checked on 30 October 2026. These are separate admissions, not a combined pass. Transport, food and optional transfers are extra.</p>
        <div class="highlight-grid">
          <article class="highlight-card"><span class="highlight-no">PARQUES DE SINTRA · ADULT 18–64</span><h3>Signature monuments</h3><p><strong>Pena Palace · Essential visit:</strong> €20. <strong>Pena Park only:</strong> €12. The optional park-to-palace transfer is an additional €4.50 return. <strong>Moorish Castle:</strong> €12. <strong>Monserrate Park and Palace:</strong> €12. <strong>National Palace of Sintra:</strong> €13. The National Palace gardens are listed as free entry.</p><a href="https://www.parquesdesintra.pt/pt/planear-a-visita/horarios-e-precos/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Check official prices and hours ↗</a></article>
          <article class="highlight-card"><span class="highlight-no">SEPARATE OPERATOR · ADULT 18–64</span><h3>Quinta da Regaleira</h3><p><strong>Adult admission:</strong> €20 (2026 tariff). The estate has its own ticketing system; tickets are valid for the selected date and time. Buy only through the official ticket office and check current access notices before travelling.</p><a href="https://www.regaleira.pt/pt/visitas" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Check official tickets, prices and hours ↗</a></article>
        </div>
        <p class="guide-disclaimer">Prices checked on 30 October 2026 against the official operators. Adult rates apply to ages 18–64; other age bands, family tickets and special conditions differ. Prices and visit formats can change. Confirm the exact product and date before paying. Sources: Parques de Sintra and Fundação Cultursintra.</p>
      </div>
    </section>


    <section class="guide-highlights" id="free-sintra">
      <div class="section-wrap">
        <p class="eyebrow">A different Sintra · Mostly free discoveries</p>
        <h2>The places you can enjoy<br><em>without buying a palace ticket.</em></h2>
        <p class="plan-lead">Some of Sintra’s best moments happen between the famous monuments. This small-town trail brings together public gardens, a free museum, a viewpoint and a remarkable historic hotel. Check opening hours before you go; “free” does not always mean open at every hour.</p>
        <div class="highlight-grid">
          <article class="highlight-card"><span class="highlight-no">FREE · MUSEUM</span><h3>Museu Anjos Teixeira</h3><p>A lovely off-the-main-route discovery dedicated to sculptors Artur and Pedro Anjos Teixeira, father and son. Look for the human and animal figures, studies and models. The museum occupies an old watermill building by the Rio do Porto, which makes the setting part of the visit too.</p><p><strong>Why stop:</strong> A genuine cultural visit, not just another photo stop.</p><p><strong>Typical hours:</strong> Tue–Fri 10:00–18:00; weekends 12:00–18:00. Closed Mondays and most public holidays.</p><p><strong>Entry:</strong> Free. Allow around 20–40 minutes as a planning estimate.</p><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=Museu+Anjos+Teixeira+Sintra" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open museum map ↗</a> · <a href="https://visitsintra.travel/pt/visitar/museus/museu-anjos-teixeira" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Official visitor details ↗</a></article>
          <article class="highlight-card"><span class="highlight-no">FREE · GARDEN</span><h3>Gardens of the National Palace</h3><p>Here is a useful detail many visitors miss: the National Palace’s gardens have free admission, even though entry to the palace interiors is ticketed. It is an easy way to enjoy a quieter corner of the royal complex without committing to the full visit.</p><p><strong>Why stop:</strong> A calm pause right in the historic centre, especially if you are saving your budget for another monument.</p><p><strong>Current published hours:</strong> 09:30–18:30; last entry 18:00. Check the official page before visiting.</p><p><strong>Entry:</strong> Free to the gardens; palace interiors require a ticket.</p><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=Jardins+Palacio+Nacional+de+Sintra" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open garden map ↗</a> · <a href="https://www.parquesdesintra.pt/pt/parques-monumentos/palacio-nacional-sintra/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Official details ↗</a></article>
          <article class="highlight-card"><span class="highlight-no">FREE · PUBLIC PARK</span><h3>Parque da Liberdade</h3><p>A green, slightly wild public garden tucked just above the Volta do Duche. Follow its winding paths among mature trees, rocks and moss, and look for the small details that make it feel like a secret garden. The paths climb, so it is not uniformly easy for everyone.</p><p><strong>Why stop:</strong> A peaceful breather close to the centre, ideal between the museum and the old town.</p><p><strong>Published hours:</strong> Seasonal, generally from 10:00; check the municipal page for the current closing time.</p><p><strong>Entry:</strong> Free.</p><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=Parque+da+Liberdade+Sintra" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open park map ↗</a> · <a href="https://visitsintra.travel/pt/visitar/parques-e-jardins/parque-da-liberdade" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Official park story and hours ↗</a></article>
          <article class="highlight-card"><span class="highlight-no">FREE · VIEWPOINT</span><h3>Miradouro do Adro de São Martinho</h3><p>This is the little viewpoint I would not want visitors to miss. From the churchyard terrace you can frame the National Palace, the white houses of the old town and, higher up, the Moorish Castle and Pena. On a clear day, the view stretches towards the coast.</p><p><strong>Why stop:</strong> One of the best quick panoramas in the historic centre, with benches for a proper pause.</p><p><strong>Best moment:</strong> Late afternoon, when the light softens over the village.</p><p><strong>Entry:</strong> Free public viewpoint.</p><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=Miradouro+do+Adro+da+Igreja+de+S+Martinho+Sintra" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open viewpoint map ↗</a> · <a href="https://visitsintra.travel/pt/visitar/miradouros-e-cascatas/miradouro-do-adro-da-igreja-de-s-martinho" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Official viewpoint details ↗</a></article>
          <article class="highlight-card"><span class="highlight-no">HISTORIC LANDMARK · HOTEL</span><h3>Lawrence’s Hotel</h3><p>Founded in 1764 as the Estalagem dos Cavaleiros, Lawrence’s is widely described as the oldest hotel on the Iberian Peninsula. It later became associated with the Englishman Lewis Lawrence and with literary Sintra: Lord Byron stayed here, and the hotel is connected to the world of Eça de Queirós’s <em>Os Maias</em>.</p><p><strong>Why stop:</strong> Notice the historic façade and imagine the generations of travellers who have passed through this street. It is a working hotel, so respect guest privacy and do not assume the interior is open to non-guests.</p><p><strong>Entry:</strong> Admire the exterior from the public street; access to hotel spaces is for guests or by arrangement.</p><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=Lawrences+Hotel+Sintra" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open hotel map ↗</a> · <a href="https://www.lawrenceshotel.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Hotel website and history ↗</a></article>
          <article class="highlight-card"><span class="highlight-no">FREE · GARDEN WALK</span><h3>Vila Sassetti</h3><p>A beautiful garden path and historic villa on the way up towards the hilltop monuments. It is a rewarding alternative to simply taking the road, with landscaped terraces and a strong sense of Sintra’s romantic garden culture.</p><p><strong>Why stop:</strong> A scenic link between the village and the hills, especially if you enjoy walking. The climb is real, and this is not a step-free shortcut.</p><p><strong>Entry:</strong> Free. Opening hours are published by Parques de Sintra and can change.</p><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=Vila+Sassetti+Sintra" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open garden map ↗</a> · <a href="https://www.parquesdesintra.pt/pt/parques-monumentos/vila-sassetti/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Official visitor details ↗</a></article>
        </div>
        <p class="guide-disclaimer">Free-entry information and opening hours checked against official visitor sources on 30 October 2026. Temporary closures, maintenance and special-event restrictions may apply. The museum is free according to Visit Sintra; the National Palace gardens are explicitly listed as free by Parques de Sintra. The Parque da Liberdade is a public municipal park.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

